---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeViewer from '../../components/CodeViewer.astro';
import { publicTokens } from '../../data/public-tokens.js';
import reference from '../generated-reference.json';
const sections=[{id:'properties',title:'Custom properties'},{id:'palette',title:'Default palette'},{id:'overrides',title:'Overrides'}];
---
<DocsLayout title="CSS tokens" active="tokens" sections={sections}>
<p class="doc-kicker">REFERENCE</p><h1>CSS tokens</h1>
<p class="doc-lead">Shared attributes are the main configuration API. Use custom properties for values that need a project-specific adjustment.</p>
<section id="properties"><h2>Custom properties</h2><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Documented CSS custom properties" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Value type</th><th scope="col">Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>{publicTokens.map(([area,name,type,description])=><tr><td>{area}</td><th scope="row"><code>{name}</code></th><td>{type}</td><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p>Other component-internal variables implement derived colours and state. Prefer the shared attributes and documented properties above; the development API may still change before beta.</p></section>
<section id="palette"><h2>Default palette: monochrome foundations and Blue Teal accent</h2><p>The values below come from the palette manifest. Choose a different coordinated set with data-palette. Tone, local theme and glass material can alter effective component colours.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Default palette values" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.keys(reference.palettes.default.light).map(name=><tr><th scope="row"><code>--re-{name}</code></th><td><code>{reference.palettes.default.light[name]}</code></td><td><code>{reference.palettes.default.dark[name]}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h3>Semantic role tokens</h3><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Semantic role values" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.keys(reference.roles.light).map(name=><tr><th scope="row"><code>--re-{name}</code></th><td><code>{reference.roles.light[name]}</code></td><td><code>{reference.roles.dark[name]}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="overrides"><h2>Override on the configured boundary</h2><p>Global application values can live on :root. Scoped overrides belong on .reva or a descendant. Explicit shared attributes can install their own local token values, so place custom overrides where they should take precedence.</p>
<CodeViewer id="accent-tokens" lang="css" label="A custom accent" code={':root {\n  --re-primary: #7041cf;\n  --re-primary-end: #5228a4;\n  --re-on-primary: #fff;\n}\n.reva.product-panel {\n  --re-container: 60rem;\n  --re-card-padding: 1.25rem;\n}'}/>
<p>Changing a colour does not automatically produce a readable palette. Review foregrounds, gradients, borders and glass backgrounds together. Opacity properties take percentages rather than decimal numbers.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/eristavi/RevaCSS/blob/main/tokens/foundation.tokens.json">Foundation token source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/eristavi/RevaCSS/blob/main/tokens/palettes.json">Eight-palette token manifest</a> · <a href="https://github.com/eristavi/RevaCSS/blob/main/tokens/options.json">Attribute option manifest</a></p></section>
</DocsLayout>
